TED4C-L COMPOSITE RIGHTS NOTICE

Version 1.1, 23 June 2026

TED4C-L contains dataset-specific contributions from the SICAGE authors together
with numeric representations derived from TED source material. The public release
does not contain readable subtitle or transcript strings. Different rights apply to
these components.

1. SICAGE contributions

To the extent the SICAGE authors own the dataset selection, organization,
dataset-specific metadata, split definitions, and documentation, they license those
contributions under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
International license (CC BY-NC 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

Attribution should identify TED4C-L and cite the SICAGE paper and repository.

2. TED source material

No rights in TED source material are granted by the SICAGE authors. TED source
content, transcripts, subtitles, and any rights that continue in representations
derived from them remain subject to the rights of TED, speakers, and other relevant
rightsholders. Users are responsible for confirming that their intended use is
permitted by the applicable rightsholders.

3. No additional permission

Possession of TED4C-L does not grant permission to use TED names, branding, source
media, transcripts, subtitles, speaker identity, or likeness beyond permission held
by the user from the applicable rightsholder. TED does not sponsor or endorse this
dataset.

4. Requested responsible use

TED4C-L is intended for non-commercial research and reproducibility. It should not be
used for biometric identification, surveillance, inference of sensitive personal
attributes, or decisions about individuals. The culture labels are broad dataset
source groups, not verified labels of nationality, ethnicity, or personal identity.

5. Disclaimer

THE DATASET IS PROVIDED AS IS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND. USERS
ARE RESPONSIBLE FOR COMPLYING WITH COPYRIGHT, PRIVACY, PERSONALITY, DATA PROTECTION,
AND OTHER APPLICABLE LAWS. THIS NOTICE IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE.
